{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לבעבור", :translit "l'ba'avur", :gloss "in order that / for the sake of"} {:he "לבעבור סבב את פני הדבר", :translit "l'ba'avur savav et pnei ha-davar", :gloss "in order to change the face of the matter"} {:he "לבעבור הביא ה' אל אבשלום את הרעה", :translit "l'ba'avur hevi' Hashem el Avshalom et ha-ra'ah", :gloss "for the sake of it the LORD brought upon Absalom the evil"} {:he "לבעבור נסות אתכם", :translit "l'ba'avur nasot etchem", :gloss "in order to test you"} {:he "ואדוני חכם כחכמת מלאך האלהים", :translit "ve-adoni chacham ke-chochmat mal'ach ha-Elohim", :gloss "and my lord is wise as the wisdom of the angel of God"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לבעבור" "לבעבור סבב את פני הדבר" "לבעבור הביא ה' אל אבשלום את הרעה"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase לבעבור נסות אתכם introduces the purpose of the theophany at Sinai as a test (Exodus 20:17). David's wisdom is praised by the woman of Tekoa in 2 Samuel 14:20: ואדני חכם כחכמת מלאך האלהים. The episode of Absalom and the woman of Tekoa is narrated in 2 Samuel 14, where לבעבור סבב את פני הדבר and לבעבור הביא ה' אל אבשלום את הרעה appear.", :sources ["Exodus 20:17" "2 Samuel 14:20" "2 Samuel 14:19" "2 Samuel 14:17"]}} {:quotes [{:he "תחטאו", :translit "techeta'u", :gloss "you shall sin"} {:he "רגזו ואל תחטאו", :translit "rigzu ve-al techeta'u", :gloss "tremble and do not sin"} {:he "בעבור תהיה יראתו על פניכם לבלתי תחטאו", :translit "ba'avur tih'yat yirato al pneichem l'vilti techeta'u", :gloss "so that His fear will be upon your faces so that you do not sin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["תחטאו" "רגזו ואל תחטאו"]}], :frame {:text "Exodus 20:17 states בעבור תהיה יראתו על פניכם לבלתי תחטאו, understood to mean that the fear of God manifest upon the face produces shame that restrains sin. Psalm 4:5 reads רגזו ואל תחטאו. The Talmud states that anyone who has shame does not quickly sin (Niddah 20b) and that anger leads one to sin, while the verse לבלתי תחטאו is read in this light (Shabbat 105b, Nedarim 22a).", :sources ["Exodus 20:17" "Psalms 4:5" "Niddah 20b" "Shabbat 105b" "Nedarim 22a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יראתו על פניכם", :translit "yirato al pneichem", :gloss "His fear upon your faces"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gematria equating יראתו על פניכם with בושת הפנים, though the second term is stated implicitly rather than written in full."}], :frame {:text "Exodus 20:17 reads בעבור תהיה יראתו על פניכם, literally 'so that His fear shall be upon your faces.' The phrase על פניכם, 'upon your faces,' read together with the Rabbinic identification of shame as a sin-restraining quality (Niddah 20b), supports reading 'fear upon the face' as referring to visible shame. The Ba'al HaTurim here encodes this reading through gematria.", :sources ["Exodus 20:17" "Niddah 20b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לבעבור" "לבעבור סבב את פני הדבר" "לבעבור הביא ה' אל אבשלום את הרעה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לבעבור", :refs ["Exodus 20:20" "2 Samuel 14:20" "2 Samuel 17:14"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לבעבור סבב את פני הדבר", :refs ["2 Samuel 14:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לבעבור הביא ה' אל אבשלום את הרעה", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["תחטאו" "רגזו ואל תחטאו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "תחטאו", :refs ["Genesis 42:22" "Exodus 20:20" "1 Samuel 14:34" "Psalms 4:5"], :n 4, :lens :exact} {:phrase "רגזו ואל תחטאו", :refs ["Psalms 4:5"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gematria equating יראתו על פניכם with בושת הפנים, though the second term is stated implicitly rather than written in full.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:10.551167090Z", :model "glm-5.2"}